    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0307" n="208" xml:id="pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/314</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-06">June 6, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference is made to the Department’s telegraphic instruction of even date<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d143-f1"/> designating Mr. Curtis T. Everett as an observer at
                    an Inter-Governmental Conference to be held at Geneva on July 2, 1936, with a
                    view to arranging a system of legal protection for refugees coming from
                    Germany.</p>
                <p>In connection with the Conference under reference, there is transmitted herewith
                    a memorandum which has been prepared in the Department for the use of Mr.
                    Everett.</p>


                <xi:include href="d143-a1.xml" xpointer="d143-a1"/>
            </div>
